      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee's_Summit%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lees Summit’s historic downtown, home to an Amtrak station, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee's_Summit%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1961 Western Electric opened a factory in Lees Summit that employed about three thousand workers within a year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee's_Summit%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lees Summit celebrates culture with annual Downtown Days, Oktoberfest, and a monthly Fourth Fridays Art Walk showcasing local artists.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee's_Summit%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Missouri Pacific Railroad line that prompted Lees Summit’s founding remains active today under Union Pacific ownership.",
